# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `make` reads `.env` and exports every value to the worker, gateway and core
# banking service. Two consequences worth knowing:
#
#   * A value here BEATS the same variable already exported in your shell.
#     Delete or comment a line to fall back to the shell.
#   * It is read as Make syntax, so keep it to plain `KEY=value`. No quotes
#     (they become part of the value), no trailing `# comment` on a value
#     line, and write a literal dollar sign as `$$`.
#
# Only the first variable is required, and only for `make demo` and
# `make fixtures`. `make test` and `make verify` run keyless under
# FIXTURE_MODE=1. Everything else below is spec §17's default, shown so the
# knobs are discoverable -- uncomment only what you are changing.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- the model and the extraction loop's bounds -----------------------------
# MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# MAX_ITERATIONS=8

# Run the extraction loop off committed fixtures instead of the live API.
# FIXTURE_MODE=0

# --- SLA timers: spec defaults, then the demo profile -----------------------
# The demo profile is what makes the timer beats watchable in a live demo;
# the defaults are what the business process would actually use.
# SLA_REMIND=3d        # demo: 30s
# SLA_ESCALATE=7d      # demo: 60s
# CLIENT_ID_SLA=1d     # demo: 45s

# --- topology ---------------------------------------------------------------
# TEMPORAL_ADDRESS=localhost:7233
# TASK_QUEUE=customer-onboarding
# CORE_BANKING_URL=http://localhost:8001
# GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:8000

# --- storage and the slow-core knob ----------------------------------------
# DOCUMENT_STORE=./.store
# OUTBOX_DIR=./outbox
# CORE_SLOW_MS=10000

# --- pacing the stubbed stages (§17.1) --------------------------------------
# The stubbed stages finish in milliseconds, so the stepper jumps 1 -> 3 before
# anyone on the call has read it. This pads steps 1, 2, 6 and 7 -- inside the
# activities, so no durable timer and no change to the replay histories.
# Multipliers vary per stage: ingest 2x, each extraction iteration 1x, send
# docs 1x, notify 0.5x. Step 2 is padded only under FIXTURE_MODE; a live model
# call is already slow. `open_account` is never padded -- its 5s timeout is the
# ambiguous-timeout beat itself (§10.1).
# 0 disables it, which is what `make test` and `make verify` run with.
# DEMO_STEP_MS=1500

# The data converter seam (spec §17, §18). `off` is the demo default.
# PAYLOAD_CODEC=off
